# IDN Site Manager | Industrial's settings (read by its service at start):
#   sudo systemctl restart idn-site-manager-industrial   after a change.
#
# What enrolment tokens tell machines to connect to: this server's address, as machines
# reach it (comma separated). Set it before making tokens.
#IDN_PUBLIC_URLS=wss://idn.example.com/idn/link,idn://idn.example.com:29206
#
# The web UI, the API and the WebSocket link (put a TLS proxy or a tunnel in front of it
# for the internet).
#IDN_HTTP=0.0.0.0:8080
#
# QUIC links from machines (UDP; "off": WebSocket only).
#IDN_QUIC=0.0.0.0:29206
#
# IDN Voice over HTTPS for handsets on the plant network (its own self-signed
# certificate, made once in the data folder; "off": none, handsets then need the tunnel),
# and over IDN's link (QUIC) on UDP at the same address ("off" turns it off too).
#IDN_VOICE_HTTPS=0.0.0.0:29203
#
# The MQTT broker for the application server ("off": MQTT over the WebSocket only). If an
# IDN Node | Industrial runs on this machine too, its local MQTT also wants 1883: give one
# of them another port (here, e.g. 0.0.0.0:8883, or [mqtt] loopback in the Node's file).
#IDN_MQTT=0.0.0.0:1883
#
# The application's API key (else one is made and kept in
# /var/lib/idn-site-manager-industrial/api.key).
#IDN_API_KEY=
